important follow question
1: (in distributes system where they are multiple instance goes -> i would store in s3 )
2:how do handle large file 2gb

  optiona:a -> in this scenario we cannot store it into the bytes (2gb->byte[]->jvm->oom)
                instead use streaming
                    try(InputStream inputStream = file.getInputStream()){
                        //stream to storage
                    }

  option:b ->use an s3 upload mechanism designed for streaming/multipart uploads

3:what if s3 is down ?
1:timeout
2:meaningful error response (503 service unavailable)

what happens if 500 mb data data upload fails in s3
-> since springBoot support multipart upload
-> divide 500 in 10 parts(chunks)
->fails at part4 (1,2,3 is already upload in s3)->we don't have to upload again
->client can retry again(don't reupload entire file)
->once all parts complete call completeMultipartUpload and s3 create the final object
follow back question what if client don't came for part4 and future?
    ->we can configure s3 lifecycle rule
     to abort incomplete multipart upload after a certain no of days

who do handle the scalability
->i would preferably use presigned URLs so the client uploads the parts directly to s3 rather
than sending the entire file through springboot

